 "notes": "The seated patient is a different person in almost every shot (hoodie man 0-3.5 s, others later, a woman at 7.5 s); 'the patient' is boxed as whoever sits and is examined in each shot. A second nurse sits in the background at 4.0-5.5 s and is not boxed. Nurse and patient overlap in the close-ups: boxes are split by a vertical line, so a strip of the patient's hoodie falls outside his box. From 6.0 s the students box covers mainly the row of heads because their bodies overlap nurse and patient. Blurred people in the background of 1.5-3.5 s are not boxed as students. At 7.5 s only the nurse's arms are visible (box at the bottom)."
